+Rules:
+- JSON numbers stay numeric tokens (1.0 → 1 in JSON, NOT "1" with quotes)
+- int 1 and float 1.0 produce identical bytes: b'1'
+- string "1" produces b'"1"' (no collision with numeric 1)
+- NO exponent notation (1e-07, 1E+20, etc.)
+- trailing zeros removed after decimal point
+- -0 canonically 0
+- NaN/Infinity hard fail
+- sorted keys
+- compact separators
+- UTF-8
+- nested dict/list correct
+
+Implementation: custom recursive encoder that never emits exponent notation.
+json.dumps is NOT used for the top-level because it can emit e-notation for floats.
